  "title": "Homemade Hummus",
  "description": "If you don't like spicy food, use paprika instead of chili powder, it makes the dish look pretty, and only slightly alters flavor.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>With or without tahini, homemade hummus made from scratch only takes 5 minutes to make. No needs to cook the <span class=\"st\">chickpeas</span>, just open a can and mix with garlic, lemon juice and olive oil! This delicious healthy snack can be serve for any occasion with pita bread or garden vegetables. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21284,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1659213095105} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21284-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Homemade Hummus</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/IMG_1026.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tIf you don't like spicy food, use paprika instead of chili powder, it makes the dish look pretty, and only slightly alters flavor.\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>1  can (400 g) garbanzo beans (chickpea)</li><li>1 lemon</li><li>2-3 cloves garlic (chopped)</li><li>Salt and freshly ground black pepper</li><li>1 Tbsp tahini (sesame paste) (optional)</li><li>3-4 Tbsp olive oil</li><li>A few pinches chili powder ((or paprika))</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Drain garbanzo beans, keep half of the juice.</li><li>In a food processor, place the chickpeas, lemon juice, garlic, salt, black pepper, tahini, chili powder and 2 Tbsp of olive oil. Mix until smooth. Add 1 or 2 Tbsp of the juice from the can (or water) to give a desired texture to the hummus.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/IMG_1020.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Transfer hummus to a serving bowl, drizzle with the rest of the olive oil and sprinkle with chili powder or paprika.\r\n<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/IMG_1030.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Appetizers</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
